00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:25.290
But I'm willing to say we're pretty much there.
但我愿意说我们已经差不多到了那个阶段了。

321
00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:26.790
We're 90% full Mindy.
我们已经有90%是完全体的明迪了。

322
00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:27.290
90% full Mindy.
90%的完全体明迪。

323
00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:28.210
I'll declare that.
我宣布这一点。

324
00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:29.470
We're 90%.
我们有90%了。

325
00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:31.470
90% full Mindy, the secret.
90%的完全体明迪，这个秘密。

326
00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:38.290
Lee told me also, just fun fact, not a fast fact, a fun fact.
李还告诉我，一个有趣的事实，不是快速事实，是趣事。

327
00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:39.510
This is super fun.
这超级有趣。

328
00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:46.210
That Lee's friend, who works in San Francisco, told him about having to do spring cleaning in his office.
李的朋友在旧金山工作，告诉他办公室里必须进行春季大扫除。

329
00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:50.130
And they put this storyline in at the very last minute.
于是他们在最后一刻加入了这个情节线。

330
00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:53.930
They did not have a lot of turnaround on this episode.
这一集的制作周期非常短。

331
00:13:53.930 --> 00:14:00.370
Once again, remember last time they told us that they barely got any kind of outline and they had to write their episode?
再说一次，还记得上次他们告诉我们，他们几乎没拿到什么大纲就得写剧本吗？

332
00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:02.930
And this time, there was this super big rush on the episode.
而这一次，这一集赶得特别急。

333
00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.790
They only had like three to four days to write it.
他们只有三四天的时间来写。

334
00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.450
Usually, you get a couple of weeks.
通常情况下，你有几周的时间。

335
00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:09.050
They had to turn it around really quickly.
他们必须非常快地完成它。

336
00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:13.150
And they needed some storyline for the whole office.
而且他们需要给整个办公室安排一些情节。

337
00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:16.490
They knew the secret storyline between Michael and Jim.
他们知道迈克尔和吉姆之间的秘密情节线。

338
00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:23.050
And they knew the storyline about Oscar and the investigation about whether or not he was really sick.
他们也知道关于奥斯卡以及调查他是否真的生病的情节线。

339
00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.450
But they needed something for the rest of us to be doing.
但他们需要给其他人找点事做。

340
00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:30.370
So, he called Mike Schur and he pitched this idea.
所以，他给迈克·舒尔打了电话，提出了这个想法。

341
00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:33.470
My friend told me that he had to do spring cleaning at their office.
我朋友告诉我，他办公室里必须进行春季大扫除。

342
00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.730
I think I could make it really funny.
我觉得我可以把它写得很有趣。

343
00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:38.190
And he wrote me and he said that Mike Schur's response was, quote,
他写信告诉我，迈克·舒尔的回应是，引用原话：

344
00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:40.230
If you have to, you have to.
如果必须做，那就做吧。

345
00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:42.910
You have to.
你必须做。

346
00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:43.550
You have to.
你必须做。

347
00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.230
If you need it, do it.
如果你需要，就去做吧。

348
00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.070
At two minutes, seven seconds.
在两分零七秒的时候。

349
00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.630
Jenna, you must have been so tickled.
珍娜，你一定觉得很有趣吧。

350
00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:52.950
This is like your favorite thing where Michael's talking and then we reveal two other people.
这就像你最喜欢的那种桥段，迈克尔在说话，然后我们揭示了另外两个人的存在。

351
00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:53.810
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

352
00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:57.410
Not only are you getting a Dwight reveal, but then you get Ryan on the floor.
不仅有德怀特的揭秘，你还能看到瑞安坐在地板上。

353
00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:01.610
And he said, Michael says, a cluttered desk is a cluttered mind.
他说，迈克尔说，杂乱的桌面意味着杂乱的思绪。

354
00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:07.510
You guys, my mom, Bertie Kinsey, would say this to me every week.
伙计们，我妈妈，伯蒂·金西，每周都会对我这么说。

355
00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:11.150
She would say, Angela, a cluttered room is a cluttered mind.
她会说，安吉拉，杂乱的房间意味着杂乱的思绪。

356
00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:13.050
Because my room would get messy.
因为我的房间总是很乱。

357
00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:17.130
And when Michael said that, I was like, oh, my God, it's my mom.
当迈克尔说那句话时，我心想，天哪，这简直是我妈。

358
00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:17.870
It's my mom.
就是我妈。

359
00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:21.050
Well, you mentioned the reveal of Ryan sitting on the floor.
嗯，你提到了瑞安坐在地板上的那个镜头。

360
00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:21.550
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

361
00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:26.430
There is a deleted scene that explains why he's sitting on the floor.
有一个删减片段解释了他为什么坐在地板上。

362
00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:28.810
And it is, he has two boxes.
当时他有两个箱子。

363
00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.310
And one says keep and one says trash.
一个写着“保留”，一个写着“丢弃”。

364
00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:37.650
And he is sitting on Michael's floor going through all of Michael's things while Michael reads a newspaper.
他坐在迈克尔的地板上，翻看迈克尔所有的东西，而迈克尔在看报纸。

365
00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:38.370
Yeah.
没错。

366
00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.730
Not cleaning at all.
根本没在清理。

367
00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:46.910
And he's like, this People magazine from 1994.
他说，这本《人物》杂志是1994年的。

368
00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:48.670
And Michael's like, keep.
迈克尔说，保留。

369
00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:49.550
Keep it.
留着吧。

370
00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.110
He's like, okay.
他说，好吧。

371
00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.490
He's like, I might do the crossword.
他说，我可能还会做上面的填字游戏。

372
00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:54.350
And he's like, it's from 1994.
他说，这可是1994年的。

373
00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.590
Michael's like, I know.
迈克尔说，我知道。

374
00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:56.210
Keep.
保留。

375
00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:58.430
There's nothing in the trash box.
丢弃的箱子里什么都没有。

376
00:15:58.570 --> 00:15:59.470
It's amazing.
太绝了。

377
00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:01.170
It's a fun little nugget.
这真是一个有趣的小花絮。

378
00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:09.590
All right, I need to talk about two minutes, 34 seconds, the very, very long stare between Dwight and Angela.
好了，我得聊聊两分三十四秒处，德怀特和安吉拉之间那段非常、非常漫长的凝视。

379
00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:09.950
Yeah.
没错。

380
00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:10.890
D'Angela.
德安吉拉。

381
00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:11.410
Yeah.
没错。

382
00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.410
I have a fan question.
我有一个粉丝提问。

383
00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:13.790
Okay.
好的。

384
00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.290
From Where Are the Turtles?
来自“海龟在哪里？”。

385
00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:15.910
Okay.
好的。

386
00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:18.630
The long stare with Dwight and Angela is so brilliant.
德怀特和安吉拉的那段长镜头凝视真是太精彩了。

387
00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:20.350
As are future stares.
以后的凝视镜头也一样。

388
00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:23.210
Is it hard to not crack up while filming those?
拍摄这些镜头时，忍住不笑很难吗？

389
00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:24.650
Angela, tell us all about it.
安吉拉，跟我们说说吧。

390
00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:25.350
Yeah.
没错。

391
00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:27.190
It's hard not to crack up.
确实很难不笑场。

392
00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:30.150
I'm sure there's tons of footage of me getting tickled.
我敢肯定，有很多我被逗笑的拍摄花絮。

393
00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.050
And also, it was so fun.
而且，这真的很有趣。

394
00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:34.330
It is so fun.
真的很有趣。

395
00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:38.070
One thing I think we do in society is we know not to stare.
我认为我们在社会中学会的一件事就是知道不要盯着别人看。

396
00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:39.110
We grow up, right?
我们长大了，对吧？

397
00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:40.870
And our parents are like, don't stare.
父母会告诉我们，别盯着人看。

398
00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:41.610
Don't stare.
别盯着看。

399
00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:50.190
And so all of a sudden, you're given permission to just stare at someone and draw it out as long as possible.
所以突然之间，你被允许可以一直盯着某人看，并且尽可能地延长这个过程。

400
00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:55.210
There were times when I thought the director was going to yell cut because I'm like, surely they're done watching.
有好几次我以为导演要喊停了，因为我心想，他们肯定已经看够了。

401
00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:56.310
Stare at each other.
互相盯着看。

402
00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:57.670
And they're like, no.
他们就说，不行。

403
00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.090
Keep a going.
继续演下去。

404
00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:00.790
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

405
00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.690
But yeah, very hard to keep a straight face.
但是没错，要忍住不笑真的很难。

406
00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:06.210
And of course, having like Kevin there watching us.
当然，还有凯文在那儿看着我们。

407
00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.170
Like, what are you doing?
就像是，你们在干什么？

408
00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:13.910
Well, some context, too, to the scene is that he comes up and says that Oscar is out sick.
嗯，这场戏还有些背景，就是他走过来，说奥斯卡病了。

409
00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.530
And says something like, that's unacceptable.
然后说了句类似“这不可接受”的话。

410
00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:16.690
And you say, I agree.
你就说，我同意。

411
00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:17.590
It's unacceptable.
这确实不可接受。

412
00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:26.130
And there is like some charged, like you both are very aroused by your agreement that this is unacceptable.
当时气氛有点微妙，你们俩因为觉得这事“不可接受”而感到非常兴奋。

413
00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:26.630
Oh, no.
噢，不。

414
00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.650
I put, we get really turned on by unacceptable behavior.
我写的是，我们对这种不可接受的行为感到非常兴奋。

415
00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:31.450
Exactly.
没错。

416
00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:32.970
Exactly.
没错。

417
00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:37.410
Jenna, I have something to point out, my lady friend.
珍娜，我得指出一点，我的好朋友。

418
00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:38.110
What is it?
什么事？

419
00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:46.510
At two minutes, 50 seconds, when Dwight says Oscar is out sick, Michael says, and on a Friday?
在两分五十秒的时候，当德怀特说奥斯卡病了，迈克尔说，“而且是在周五？”

420
00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:48.650
It's Friday!
是周五啊！

421
00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:50.270
Again, a Friday!
又是一个周五！

422
00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.650
And no one is dressed casually.
而且没人穿休闲装。

423
00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:53.570
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

424
00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.490
Thank you for catching that.
谢谢你发现了这一点。

425
00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:56.150
Yeah.
是啊。

426
00:17:58.490 --> 00:17:59.910
I don't even know what to do with that.
我甚至不知道该怎么处理这个。

427
00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.450
I don't even know what to say about it.
我甚至不知道该说什么好。

428
00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:01.630
I don't know what to do with that.
我不知道该怎么处理这个。

429
00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:02.830
I don't know what to say about it.
我不知道该说什么好。

430
00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:06.490
But four minutes, nine seconds, Pam and Kelly.
但在四分零九秒，帕姆和凯莉那儿。

431
00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:08.690
Pam is planning her wedding.
帕姆正在筹备她的婚礼。

432
00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:11.170
Kelly asks to be a bridesmaid.
凯莉请求当伴娘。

433
00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:12.650
That is hilarious.
那太搞笑了。

434
00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.430
I love that so much.
我太喜欢那个片段了。

435
00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:15.790
Like, who has the audacity?
就是说，谁会有这种厚脸皮？

436
00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:18.630
Like, not even a really good friend to be like, oh, my God, can I be in your wedding?
甚至连好朋友都算不上，就敢说“天哪，我能参加你的婚礼吗？”

437
00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.450
And she's like, you don't have to answer now.
然后她还说，“你不用现在回答”。

438
00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:26.830
There's also so much going on in the scene because Pam takes her hair down and she floofs it out.
那场戏里还有很多细节，因为帕姆把头发放下来，还抓蓬松了。

439
00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:31.430
And you can see Jim in the background over Kelly's shoulder.
你可以看到吉姆在背景里，就在凯莉的肩膀后面。

440
00:18:31.430 --> 00:18:33.090
Poor Jim is what I wrote.
我写的是“可怜的吉姆”。

441
00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:33.550
Poor Jim.
可怜的吉姆。

442
00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:34.210
Oh, poor Jim.
噢，可怜的吉姆。

443
00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:39.110
And then, you know, Michael comes out of his office and has to make a comment.
然后，你知道，迈克尔从办公室出来，必须得评论一下。

444
00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:40.790
This was a tricky one to film.
这一场戏拍起来很棘手。

445
00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:48.830
And I always want to point these scenes out because I just think they're really great examples of the choreography of our director, our camera operators.
我总是想指出这些场景，因为我觉得它们是导演和摄影师调度能力的绝佳体现。

446
00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:51.290
It's really something special to capture this stuff.
能捕捉到这些内容真的很特别。

447
00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:55.110
Well, Michael says you should leave your hair down more because it's sexier.
迈克尔说你应该多把头发放下来，因为那样更性感。

448
00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:58.790
And then he walks past Jim and he goes, oh, this must be so hard on you.
然后他走过吉姆身边，说了句，“噢，这对你来说一定很难受吧”。

449
00:18:59.070 --> 00:18:59.310
Yeah.
是啊。

450
00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:01.870
Way to make it all worse, Michael.
迈克尔，你真是让情况变得更糟了。

451
00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:08.870
Then we move on to a spy shot conversation between Jim and Michael in Michael's office.
接下来我们转到吉姆和迈克尔在迈克尔办公室里的一段秘密谈话。

452
00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:16.310
This is when Michael finds out that he is the only person who knows about Jim's feelings for Pam.
这是迈克尔发现他是唯一知道吉姆对帕姆有感情的人的时候。

453
00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:21.510
And I want you to notice at 4 minutes, 57 seconds, Michael is playing with a golf ball.
我想请大家注意在4分57秒时，迈克尔在玩一个高尔夫球。

454
00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:22.550
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

455
00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:23.130
He is.
确实是。

456
00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:26.010
And that is because of that cold open that we cut out.
那是因为我们剪掉的那个开场戏。

457
00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:26.450
Right.
对。

458
00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:28.550
And he had all the golf stuff in his office.
他当时办公室里全是高尔夫球具。

459
00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:28.850
Yeah.
是啊。

460
00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:29.390
Right.
没错。

461
00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:33.830
Well, Michael says something in this scene that I thought was so great.
迈克尔在这一幕里说的话我觉得太棒了。

462
00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:34.910
It's his talking head.
那是他的个人采访镜头。

463
00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:36.410
And Steve is so brilliant in it.
史蒂夫演得真是太精彩了。

464
00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:42.010
He just talks about how special it is, you know, obviously that Jim shared with him and what good friends they are, blah, blah, blah.
他一直在说这有多特别，你知道的，显然是吉姆跟他分享了秘密，他们关系有多好之类的，巴拉巴拉。

465
00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:46.150
But his last sentence just made me laugh.
但他最后那句话真的把我逗笑了。

466
00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:50.870
He goes, and it is why I intend on keeping that secret for as long as I possibly can.
他说，这就是为什么我打算尽可能久地保守这个秘密。

467
00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:55.190
He totally owns that he sucks at keeping a secret.
他完全承认自己不擅长保守秘密。

468
00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:59.850
You guys, my dad was someone who absolutely could not hold on to information.
伙计们，我爸爸就是那种绝对藏不住事的人。

469
00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:05.310
Now, he was a wonderful friend and father and confidant, all of those things.
他是个很棒的朋友、父亲和知己，所有这些他都做得很好。

470
00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:15.230
But if there was, like, some great information, there was no way he could not, like, tell you or it just – it would be all over his face.
但如果有什么重大消息，他根本没法忍住不告诉你，或者说——这全写在他脸上了。

471
00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:15.650
Yeah.
是啊。

472
00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:18.690
Well, I had no poker face when Steve said that.
史蒂夫说那话的时候，我完全没法保持扑克脸。

473
00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:24.570
I just sort of chuckled and thought of my dad and how hard it was for him to, like, keep any news from us.
我只是笑了笑，想到了我爸爸，想到他要对我们隐瞒任何消息有多困难。

474
00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:26.950
Are you good with secrets or are you more like your dad?
你擅长保守秘密吗？还是说你更像你爸爸？

475
00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:28.750
I think I'm good.
我觉得我挺擅长的。

476
00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:29.810
I think I'm good.
我觉得我挺擅长的。

477
00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.510
I don't know, Jenna.
我不知道，珍娜。

478
00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:32.630
You've known me a long time.
你认识我很久了。

479
00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:33.810
I think you're good.
我觉得你挺擅长的。

480
00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:34.310
Yeah.
是啊。

481
00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:36.430
We had a fan question, actually.
其实我们有个粉丝提问。

482
00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:40.950
It was Shanice who asked, are you two good at keeping secrets?
是莎妮丝问的，你们俩擅长保守秘密吗？

483
00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:46.190
Do you have that one person that you just have to share it with because you trust them and that's okay?
你们有没有那种必须分享秘密的人，因为你信任他们，所以那样做没关系？

484
00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:47.030
Yeah.
有。

485
00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:47.510
Yeah.
有。

486
00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:50.870
Well, anyone who tells me anything should know that I'm going to tell Jenna.
嗯，任何告诉我事情的人都应该知道，我肯定会告诉珍娜。

487
00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:54.030
I am.
我会的。

488
00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:57.830
Unless you – if you're like, hey, you can't say this to anyone.
除非你——如果你说，嘿，你不能告诉任何人。

489
00:20:57.930 --> 00:20:58.370
Yeah.
是啊。

490
00:20:58.830 --> 00:20:59.070
Okay.
好吧。

491
00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:00.810
And then I'm going to tell my husband.
然后我还是会告诉我丈夫。

492
00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:02.190
I tell my husband everything.
我什么都告诉我丈夫。

493
00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:07.830
Like, you have to really say, all right, you can't – and then I probably will at some point tell you or my husband.
所以你真的得说，好吧，你不能——即便如此，我可能迟早还是会告诉你或者我丈夫。

494
00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.210
So even if they tell you not to.
所以即使他们让你别说。

495
00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:11.610
I might sit on it for a bit.
我可能会先憋一会儿。

496
00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:18.390
But eventually, I mean, I honestly – I'm sitting here like thinking like, I don't know, Jenna.
但最终，我是说，我老实说——我坐在这儿想，我不知道，珍娜。

497
00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:20.710
I pretty much have to download everything to you.
我基本上必须把所有事情都向你倾诉。

498
00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:22.470
It's like kind of how I process information.
这算是我处理信息的一种方式吧。

499
00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:24.330
I receive information.
我接收信息。

500
00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:25.910
I know how I feel about it.
我知道我对它的感受。

501
00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:31.190
But then, like, it either becomes more real or more clear to me once I share it with you or Josh.
但后来，一旦我把它分享给你或乔什，它对我来说要么变得更真实，要么变得更清晰。

502
00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:32.730
I feel the same way.
我有同感。

503
00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:36.030
You and Lee are the two people that I tell everything to.
你和李是我什么都说的两个人。

504
00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:44.050
So if someone tells me something in confidence, I assume they know that they are telling me, Angela, and Lee simultaneously.
所以如果有人私下告诉我什么事，我默认他们知道他们是在同时告诉我和安吉拉，还有李。

505
00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:45.870
My best friend and my husband.
我最好的朋友和我丈夫。

506
00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:46.510
That's right.
没错。

507
00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:53.070
However, I will say there are things that you have told me, Angela, that I have not shared with Lee.
不过，我得说，安吉拉，有些你告诉我的事，我并没有告诉李。

508
00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:56.650
And there are things that Lee has told me that I have not shared with you.
同样，有些李告诉我的事，我也没告诉你。

509
00:21:56.950 --> 00:21:57.070
Same.
我也是。

510
00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:58.510
So I do –
所以我确实——

511
00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:01.710
Those two people are like – they get special treatment.
那两个人就像是——他们享受特殊待遇。

512
00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:02.850
Yes, that's right.
是的，没错。

513
00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:08.050
All the rest of y'all, just know I am blabbing to Lee and Angela if you told me.
至于你们其他人，只要知道如果你们告诉了我什么，我肯定会转头告诉李和安吉拉。

514
00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:08.350
Yeah.
没错。

515
00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:10.570
Unless you specifically tell me not to.
除非你明确告诉我不要说。

516
00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:15.450
And then, similar to you, Angela, I will sit on it for a bit and then tell them anyway.
然后，和你一样，安吉拉，我会先憋一会儿，但最后还是会告诉他们。

517
00:22:15.710 --> 00:22:16.050
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

518
00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:24.450
At 5 minutes, 43 seconds, Dwight goes up to Ryan and he wants, you know, Ryan basically to take over the spring cleaning stuff.
在5分43秒时，德怀特走到瑞安面前，他想，你知道的，他基本上是想让瑞安接手春季大扫除的事。

519
00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:24.670
Yeah.
没错。

520
00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:26.430
Because he's got this investigation to conduct.
因为他要进行一项调查。

521
00:22:26.730 --> 00:22:32.930
Now, I did a ton of scenes with Rainn Wilson and Rainn loves a prop.
我跟雷恩·威尔森拍过很多戏，雷恩特别喜欢用道具。

522
00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:36.110
And once he gets a prop, he's very attached to a prop.
一旦他拿到道具，就会对它产生很深的感情。

523
00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:39.310
So he did this thing in this scene that made me laugh so hard.
所以他在这一幕里做了一个动作，让我笑得不行。

524
00:22:39.450 --> 00:22:40.550
He walks up to Ryan.
他走向瑞安。

525
00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:42.650
He has his little notepad he's writing in.
他手里拿着记事本在写东西。

526
00:22:42.850 --> 00:22:43.010
Yeah.
没错。

527
00:22:43.010 --> 00:22:48.890
And as he walks up to Ryan, he takes it out of his jacket pocket and he flashes it at Ryan as if it's like a badge.
当他走向瑞安时，他从夹克口袋里掏出本子，像亮出徽章一样在瑞安面前晃了一下。

528
00:22:49.850 --> 00:22:51.050
You have to watch it.
你们一定要看一看。

529
00:22:51.130 --> 00:22:52.530
It's this very subtle move.
那是一个非常微妙的动作。

530
00:22:52.630 --> 00:22:53.210
It's just a notepad.
那只是个记事本。

531
00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:57.490
It looks like one of those notepads that you win for 200 tickets at Chuck E.
看起来就像那种在查克芝士店用200张奖券换来的记事本。

532
00:22:57.570 --> 00:22:57.730
Cheese.
没错。

533
00:22:58.210 --> 00:22:58.610
Exactly.
就是这样。

534
00:22:58.950 --> 00:22:59.110
Yeah.
没错。

535
00:22:59.290 --> 00:22:59.550
Exactly.
就是这样。

536
00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:01.550
So he's like, I'm conducting a little investigation.
所以他就像是说，我正在进行一项小调查。

537
00:23:01.550 --> 00:23:03.050
He flashes the notepad.
他晃了晃记事本。

538
00:23:03.210 --> 00:23:07.670
Like that is going to be like, oh, okay, this is legit.
好像那样就能让对方觉得，哦，好吧，这是正经事。

539
00:23:08.010 --> 00:23:08.230
Yeah.
没错。

540
00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:09.030
To Ryan.
对瑞安来说。

541
00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:11.070
And Ryan, of course, is just like, ugh.
而瑞安当然就是一副，呃，受不了的样子。

542
00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:15.550
So then we move to the vending machines.
然后我们转到自动售货机那边。

543
00:23:15.850 --> 00:23:16.290
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

544
00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:24.530
Michael is trying to talk to Jim more about his love of Pam at the vending machines and Stanley enters.
迈克尔在自动售货机旁试图跟吉姆多聊聊他喜欢帕姆的事，这时斯坦利进来了。

545
00:23:25.030 --> 00:23:26.030
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

546
00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:30.890
And Stanley is taking forever to pick a beverage.
斯坦利选饮料选了半天。

547
00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:31.430
He is.
确实是。

548
00:23:31.530 --> 00:23:32.310
Just forever.
简直太久了。

549
00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:34.230
And he's in the way.
而且他还挡路。

550
00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:38.490
And Michael is trying so much to capitalize on this bonding time with Jim.
迈克尔正拼命想利用这段时间跟吉姆拉近关系。

551
00:23:38.690 --> 00:23:39.990
He's like, we're best friends.
他就像是说，我们是最好的朋友。

552
00:23:39.990 --> 00:23:40.790
We share secrets.
我们分享秘密。

553
00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:43.850
I just want to spend now as much time as possible with him.
我只是想现在尽可能多地和他待在一起。

554
00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:46.730
I want to chat about his love for Pam.
我想聊聊他对帕姆的爱。

555
00:23:46.950 --> 00:23:48.750
I want him to know I'm a great friend.
我想让他知道我是一个很好的朋友。

556
00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:57.430
At the end of that scene, Michael just picks an item for Stanley, and it's peach iced tea.
在那场戏的结尾，迈克尔随手给斯坦利选了一样东西，是桃子味冰茶。

557
00:23:57.630 --> 00:24:00.430
And then Steve says, you're going to hate it.
然后史蒂夫说，你会讨厌它的。

558
00:24:01.110 --> 00:24:02.450
That was improvised.
那是即兴发挥的。

559
00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:10.590
And that was a moment that a lot of people wrote in about when I asked, what do you want us to talk about for this moment?
当我问大家想让我们聊聊哪个片段时，很多人都提到了那一幕。

560
00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:12.070
It was the peach iced tea.
就是桃子味冰茶那一幕。

561
00:24:12.250 --> 00:24:12.930
You're going to hate it.
你会讨厌它的。

562
00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:14.310
And it was an improvised moment.
那是一个即兴发挥的瞬间。

563
00:24:14.310 --> 00:24:14.990
It was so great.
太棒了。

564
00:24:15.130 --> 00:24:19.110
And also in that scene, John could not stop laughing.
而且在那场戏里，约翰根本停不下来笑。

565
00:24:19.510 --> 00:24:20.790
He could not stop laughing.
他笑得停不下来。

566
00:24:20.930 --> 00:24:24.850
This whole episode, he had to spend a lot of time with Steve doing scenes.
整集里，他花了很多时间和史蒂夫演对手戏。

567
00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:26.710
And John really loses it.
约翰真的笑场了。

568
00:24:27.470 --> 00:24:29.090
So this was one of those scenes.
所以这就是其中一场戏。

569
00:24:29.390 --> 00:24:31.590
John, when he loses it, his whole body collapses.
约翰笑场的时候，整个人都会瘫软下去。

570
00:24:31.950 --> 00:24:32.390
Yeah.
没错。

571
00:24:32.530 --> 00:24:33.890
He just becomes a noodle.
他就像变成了一根面条。

572
00:24:33.890 --> 00:24:39.510
At 6 minutes, 58 seconds, my background observers out there, I need your help.
在6分58秒处，各位背景观察员，我需要你们的帮助。

573
00:24:40.350 --> 00:24:42.630
Dwight is calling Oscar again.
德怀特又在给奥斯卡打电话了。

574
00:24:43.170 --> 00:24:43.910
Poor Oscar.
可怜的奥斯卡。

575
00:24:44.110 --> 00:24:45.710
Dwight's just like calling him like crazy.
德怀特简直像疯了一样给他打电话。

576
00:24:46.130 --> 00:24:49.470
But as he's sitting on his desk, he's on the phone.
但他坐在办公桌前打电话的时候。

577
00:24:50.610 --> 00:24:53.230
Behind him, okay, so the hand that's holding the phone.
在他身后，好吧，就是拿着电话的那只手。

578
00:24:53.410 --> 00:24:53.630
Okay.
好的。

579
00:24:53.630 --> 00:24:54.790
Look at the hand holding the phone.
看看拿着电话的那只手。

580
00:24:54.930 --> 00:24:56.350
Look behind his hand.
看看他手后面。

581
00:24:56.550 --> 00:24:58.710
It's like a file cabinet next to Phyllis's desk.
那是菲利斯桌子旁的一个文件柜。

582
00:24:58.930 --> 00:25:02.070
There is a hairy object.
有一个毛茸茸的东西。

583
00:25:02.490 --> 00:25:04.950
It's a black, hairy object.
那是一个黑色的、毛茸茸的东西。

584
00:25:05.710 --> 00:25:06.670
What is it?
那是什么？

585
00:25:07.150 --> 00:25:10.470
Look, wait, Sam, can you pull up 6 minutes, 58 seconds?
看，等等，萨姆，你能调到6分58秒吗？

586
00:25:10.830 --> 00:25:12.530
I kind of need Jenna to see it.
我得让珍娜看看。

587
00:25:12.730 --> 00:25:13.410
There it is.
就在那儿。

588
00:25:13.550 --> 00:25:14.150
You got it.
你找到了。

589
00:25:14.210 --> 00:25:14.650
Look at it.
看着它。

590
00:25:14.650 --> 00:25:14.850
What?
什么？

591
00:25:14.950 --> 00:25:15.770
I see nothing.
我什么都没看到。

592
00:25:15.770 --> 00:25:16.610
What are you talking about?
你在说什么？

593
00:25:16.690 --> 00:25:16.990
What?
什么？

594
00:25:17.050 --> 00:25:17.970
What is that?
那是什么？

595
00:25:18.210 --> 00:25:19.230
What is that?
那是什么？

596
00:25:19.230 --> 00:25:21.510
It looks like a wig on a wig stand.
看起来像是一个假发架上的假发。

597
00:25:21.630 --> 00:25:22.470
I know.
我知道。

598
00:25:22.730 --> 00:25:24.710
On the file cabinet next to Phyllis.
就在菲利斯旁边的文件柜上。

599
00:25:24.870 --> 00:25:27.990
I'm going to get up, and I'm going to physically look closer.
我要站起来，亲自凑近看看。

600
00:25:28.250 --> 00:25:30.090
Okay, we've looked at it, and Jenna said she-
好了，我们看过了，珍娜说她——

601
00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:31.890
I know what it is, and look at what Cody is holding.
我知道那是什么，看看科迪手里拿的是什么。

602
00:25:32.070 --> 00:25:33.430
In the booth, look through the window.
在导播间里，往窗户那边看。

603
00:25:33.570 --> 00:25:34.030
Do you see Cody?
你看到科迪了吗？

604
00:25:34.250 --> 00:25:34.910
Cody's our producer.
科迪是我们的制片人。

605
00:25:35.190 --> 00:25:36.330
Yeah, what is that thing?
没错，那玩意儿是什么？

606
00:25:36.470 --> 00:25:37.330
A feather duster.
鸡毛掸子。

607
00:25:37.650 --> 00:25:38.110
Stop it.
别闹了。

608
00:25:38.170 --> 00:25:38.890
Are you sure?
你确定吗？

609
00:25:39.170 --> 00:25:39.910
Feather duster.
鸡毛掸子。

610
00:25:40.330 --> 00:25:40.610
Really?
真的吗？

611
00:25:40.850 --> 00:25:41.010
Yeah.
真的。

612
00:25:41.630 --> 00:25:45.250
I think Phyllis has a feather duster as part of her spring cleaning, and I think that's
我觉得菲利斯春季大扫除的时候会用到鸡毛掸子，我觉得那就是

613
00:25:45.250 --> 00:25:45.790
what it is.
它了。

614
00:25:45.910 --> 00:25:47.230
Oh, that's a good call.
噢，你说得有道理。

615
00:25:47.790 --> 00:25:49.930
And also, Cody, where the heck are you-
还有，科迪，你到底在哪儿——

616
00:25:49.930 --> 00:25:52.410
Yeah, Cody, where did you get a feather duster just now?
没错，科迪，你刚才从哪儿弄来的鸡毛掸子？

617
00:25:52.490 --> 00:25:54.070
How's it just like, you're like, oh, wait a second.
怎么就感觉，你就像是，噢，等一下。

618
00:25:54.070 --> 00:25:58.730
It's like your carrot top, and you have a trunk full of random props.
就像卡罗特·托普一样，你的后备箱里装满了各种随机道具。

619
00:25:59.430 --> 00:26:01.230
Guys, Cody is a little bit like me.
伙计们，科迪有点像我。

620
00:26:01.430 --> 00:26:05.670
I think she is very organized and structured, and I believe she might walk around with a feather
我觉得她非常有条理、有规划，我相信她可能随身带着一把鸡毛

621
00:26:05.670 --> 00:26:05.990
duster.
掸子。

622
00:26:06.230 --> 00:26:07.670
Well, we've never seen it before.
好吧，我们以前从没见过。

623
00:26:07.750 --> 00:26:08.710
Where is she keeping it?
她把它藏哪儿了？

624
00:26:09.110 --> 00:26:09.910
Oh, my God.
天哪。

625
00:26:10.490 --> 00:26:10.830
All right.
好吧。

626
00:26:11.430 --> 00:26:11.830
Sorry.
抱歉。

627
00:26:12.030 --> 00:26:15.490
Sorry to take us down that road, but that was making me crazy last night.
抱歉把话题扯远了，但昨晚那事儿真让我抓狂。

628
00:26:15.490 --> 00:26:20.850
At seven minutes, 34 seconds, again, Michael, desperate to connect more with Jim.
在7分34秒处，迈克尔又一次渴望与吉姆建立更多联系。

629
00:26:21.050 --> 00:26:22.970
He's so excited about having a friend.
他因为交到了朋友而感到非常兴奋。

630
00:26:22.970 --> 00:26:24.750
He's following him around like a little puppy.
他像只小狗一样跟在吉姆身后。

631
00:26:24.930 --> 00:26:30.190
He is, and he walks up to him, and he goes, it's grape soda, because he got a grape soda,
确实，他走过去对他说，这是葡萄汽水，因为他也买了一瓶葡萄汽水，

